[{:db/id "q-80133/selection/5454853a817db13094918bdbe0e10a99656ff85367ab90ccd985c0d49438056b" :answer/id #uuid "bbcf352f-f2e7-5324-bb0d-d84ac79366d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80133/selection/1561acf2ee071f0d90b9e55c396cbf606ddad94050e0ef7511efcf5375286f0b" :answer/id #uuid "43ebdc72-c722-5f07-ae01-db469ae6b665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80133/selection/ec508878edfd1ac72232e580f5c036112ed6f0700297167c1140ceff806513c6" :answer/id #uuid "a45bb909-9087-5874-b23d-51114a3e7825" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80133/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51" :answer/id #uuid "ca6a4fb8-2db0-59c7-8419-506b1942ff19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80133/selection/bf31f50c9346bb27875cd964dc305f7f9c7b78104efc378f965ed284ca0752aa" :answer/id #uuid "e9fb57c0-f43d-5c26-b6e3-6af15bbdc903" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80133/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db73b152-d743-5e5a-9775-99aef07dfeb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80133/selection/1561acf2ee071f0d90b9e55c396cbf606ddad94050e0ef7511efcf5375286f0b" :answer-field/choices ["q-80133/selection/5454853a817db13094918bdbe0e10a99656ff85367ab90ccd985c0d49438056b" "q-80133/selection/1561acf2ee071f0d90b9e55c396cbf606ddad94050e0ef7511efcf5375286f0b" "q-80133/selection/ec508878edfd1ac72232e580f5c036112ed6f0700297167c1140ceff806513c6" "q-80133/selection/3b28495977b1653d3b265084c301e2471a25911cfc996ab9fb4d1bd2f087ac51" "q-80133/selection/bf31f50c9346bb27875cd964dc305f7f9c7b78104efc378f965ed284ca0752aa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80133" :question/id #uuid "9dc5cfec-844b-5c04-a039-53f657410565" :question/math-academy-id "q-80133" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =5 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80133/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80133"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147/selection/018f16d8966eb0c0c869a46f49c557938f87a69a92cb8abf72ae731b880dffc0" :answer/id #uuid "fe968fbe-d97d-504c-b62e-527278272744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147/selection/44fb084353a202677cdf769958bbb1636436361868503b3bfab461e75b85e854" :answer/id #uuid "c74cb847-af86-546c-a94c-daee7590d07d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.854)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147/selection/12ab9dba3c177c010ff34489a9c2ac2b36fa279649f730ec5fc16d2e65ea9b73" :answer/id #uuid "c7f0e66f-9dfb-5d78-b659-a4fae80d7f1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.156)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147/selection/fe49660f337e0a4484e3bbe1640ae94ff655aae92960b09aa2d53133e783b489" :answer/id #uuid "79bca67a-6243-5257-b2e0-cd8c682f2588" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.054)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147/selection/e3d726b2d350c74aca2d855a96dfda422c1784f7ec1a142363c8fa8f92cacc3d" :answer/id #uuid "5df9f194-a06d-5fe6-a71d-aa94e6598893" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.916)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d3a0c80-1834-5558-a1e9-38a21bc6e1be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80147/selection/018f16d8966eb0c0c869a46f49c557938f87a69a92cb8abf72ae731b880dffc0" :answer-field/choices ["q-80147/selection/018f16d8966eb0c0c869a46f49c557938f87a69a92cb8abf72ae731b880dffc0" "q-80147/selection/44fb084353a202677cdf769958bbb1636436361868503b3bfab461e75b85e854" "q-80147/selection/12ab9dba3c177c010ff34489a9c2ac2b36fa279649f730ec5fc16d2e65ea9b73" "q-80147/selection/fe49660f337e0a4484e3bbe1640ae94ff655aae92960b09aa2d53133e783b489" "q-80147/selection/e3d726b2d350c74aca2d855a96dfda422c1784f7ec1a142363c8fa8f92cacc3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80147" :question/id #uuid "da754d54-7ad0-5021-82bb-f04c6fa332b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-80147" :question/problem "$2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)≈$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =0.955\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =8+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =24 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-80147/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80147"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274608/field-1/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6" :answer/id #uuid "276e148f-0b35-5396-a427-5625a3fbc2ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274608/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb86c23b-2ad0-5c04-87a3-d219eb6377b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274608/field-1/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-274608/field-1/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274608" :question/id #uuid "c890a749-89bd-5f7a-8848-aae7a952ef6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-274608" :question/problem "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2)^{2}+(5)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-274608/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f12d8028-2520-5706-ba49-d67935036af6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327723/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "28ce03b8-392b-50fd-a2c4-578ecab26b4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327723/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "f98025fc-aa81-5dec-81bd-9f432e1ffcac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327723/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5261daf7-2e11-5371-b298-a3a1783a92a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327723/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-327723/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-327723/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327723" :question/id #uuid "855c97cf-010b-5c84-8d20-2273c5c0a4d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-327723" :question/problem "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-327723/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c40813-d2aa-5eff-b5dc-69a2f916f865"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327982/field-1/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6" :answer/id #uuid "6bf49106-353a-5c48-97c4-220a494985c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327982/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "015e8759-b0e1-55c9-8bee-20101d2f06a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327982/field-1/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-327982/field-1/54e998e2b9613564e4db88fa790dea7921b62f7340b79dc7ba61859b983ac0f6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327982/field-2/87e856cdd1283a6b81b66b6b0026dbbdaec194b8878dd2995b976b1db27e728f" :answer/id #uuid "291b63a1-c462-5e75-ab6e-3fc4a5607f78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.381" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327982/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbe94955-29c5-52cc-a713-bbd150fc22c3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327982/field-2/87e856cdd1283a6b81b66b6b0026dbbdaec194b8878dd2995b976b1db27e728f" :answer-field/choices ["q-327982/field-2/87e856cdd1283a6b81b66b6b0026dbbdaec194b8878dd2995b976b1db27e728f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327982" :question/id #uuid "71d47ce5-da63-5fd4-a040-f991c91be8f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-327982" :question/problem "Express $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude–phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.381\\,\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFor the amplitude,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ & ={2}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{29}sin\\,(x-0.381).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327982/field-1" "q-327982/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65b4e8e7-e558-50e7-a1ec-37a6eff77e87"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327982"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
